    <dashboard enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Dashboard 3'>
      <style />
      <size maxheight='900' maxwidth='1400' minheight='900' minwidth='1400' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98222' id='3' param='horz' type-v2='layout-flow' w='49429' x='50000' y='889'>
            <zone h='98222' id='6' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='49429' x='50000' y='889'>
              <zone h='9000' id='8' name='Revenue  By State' pane-specification-id='0' param='[federated.042lfkd0rqc4py103ezla0qwvlf5].[sum:Calculation_0119064662609923:qk]' type-v2='color' w='49429' x='50000' y='889'>
                <zone-style>
                  <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                  <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                </zone-style>
              </zone>
              <zone forceUpdate='true' h='84222' id='9' type-v2='text' w='49429' x='50000' y='9889'>
                <formatted-text>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>Key Observations</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>Revenue is spread across states in a fairly narrow band rather than concentrated in one place. Rajasthan leads at 749,439,187, followed closely by Punjab (593,149,393), Gujarat (592,819,800), and Maharashtra (roughly 599M). A second tier, Delhi, West Bengal, Karnataka, and Tamil Nadu, sits between 439M and 469M.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>The Rajasthan detail box adds useful texture: 25,440 total orders at an average order value of 24,157.8, meaning Rajasthan&apos;s lead comes from a genuine mix of strong order volume and healthy order size, not just one or the other.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>Why This Matters</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>This is the geographic counterpart to the category concentration problem seen earlier, and it tells the opposite story. Where Electronics represents dangerous single-category dependency, no single state comes close to that kind of dominance here. The gap between the top state (Rajasthan) and the lowest shown state (Karnataka) is roughly 1.7x, compared to over 230x between Electronics and Books at the category level.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>That difference matters strategically: it means the business&apos;s revenue engine is not geographically fragile. If demand softened in any one state, the impact on total revenue would be modest, unlike the outsized risk carried by Electronics. This chart effectively rules out geography as a source of concentration risk, letting the rest of the analysis focus specifically on category and discounting behavior as the real driver of the profitability problem.</run>
                </formatted-text>
                <zone-style>
                  <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                  <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                </zone-style>
              </zone>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone h='98222' id='5' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='49429' x='571' y='889'>
            <zone h='98222' id='7' name='Revenue  By State' w='49429' x='571' y='889'>
              <layout-cache minheight='250' type-h='scalable' type-w='fixed' />
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='4' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <devicelayouts>
        <devicelayout auto-generated='true' name='Phone'>
          <size maxheight='700' minheight='700' sizing-mode='vscroll' />
          <zones>
            <zone h='100000' id='27' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
              <zone h='84000' id='26' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='84000' x='8000' y='8000'>
                <zone fixed-size='280' h='98222' id='7' is-fixed='true' name='Revenue  By State' w='49429' x='571' y='889'>
                  <layout-cache minheight='250' type-h='scalable' type-w='fixed' />
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone h='9000' id='8' name='Revenue  By State' pane-specification-id='0' param='[federated.042lfkd0rqc4py103ezla0qwvlf5].[sum:Calculation_0119064662609923:qk]' type-v2='color' w='49429' x='50000' y='889'>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='84222' id='9' type-v2='text' w='49429' x='50000' y='9889'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>Key Observations</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>Revenue is spread across states in a fairly narrow band rather than concentrated in one place. Rajasthan leads at 749,439,187, followed closely by Punjab (593,149,393), Gujarat (592,819,800), and Maharashtra (roughly 599M). A second tier, Delhi, West Bengal, Karnataka, and Tamil Nadu, sits between 439M and 469M.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>The Rajasthan detail box adds useful texture: 25,440 total orders at an average order value of 24,157.8, meaning Rajasthan&apos;s lead comes from a genuine mix of strong order volume and healthy order size, not just one or the other.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>Why This Matters</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>This is the geographic counterpart to the category concentration problem seen earlier, and it tells the opposite story. Where Electronics represents dangerous single-category dependency, no single state comes close to that kind of dominance here. The gap between the top state (Rajasthan) and the lowest shown state (Karnataka) is roughly 1.7x, compared to over 230x between Electronics and Books at the category level.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12'>That difference matters strategically: it means the business&apos;s revenue engine is not geographically fragile. If demand softened in any one state, the impact on total revenue would be modest, unlike the outsized risk carried by Electronics. This chart effectively rules out geography as a source of concentration risk, letting the rest of the analysis focus specifically on category and discounting behavior as the real driver of the profitability problem.</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
              </zone>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='8' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
          </zones>
        </devicelayout>
      </devicelayouts>
      <simple-id uuid='{2EFFFB55-ABFF-472A-A6B8-D69C44DCB5A2}' />
    </dashboard>
    <dashboard enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Dashboard 4'>
