              <zone fixed-size='464' forceUpdate='true' h='47200' id='11' is-fixed='true' type-v2='text' w='49500' x='50000' y='48600'>
                <formatted-text>
                  <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#f9a655' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='12' underline='true'>KEY INSIGHTS:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='10'>Electronics sits alone in a dangerous quadrant: highest revenue, highest discount, and the only negative profit margin.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='10'>Top panel, Revenue: Electronics towers at roughly 60K average net revenue per unit, more than double Home.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='10'>Middle panel, Discount: Electronics also carries by far the steepest average discount amount, around 20K, while every other category sits below 5K.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='10'>Bottom panel, Profit Margin: Electronics is the only category with a negative estimated margin, sitting below zero while every other category is comfortably positive.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='10'>Why this matters: high discounting is compressing Electronics&apos; margin into negative territory, despite it generating the most revenue. The category that looks most successful by revenue is actually the least sustainable by profitability.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='10'>Contrast case, Beauty: low revenue, minimal discount, and the highest profit margin — proving the relationship isn&apos;t inherent to the business model, it&apos;s category-specific behavior.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='10'>in this: since margin relies on an assumed cost ratio, the exact figure could shift, but Electronics ranking lowest is robust, since it lines up with its much larger discount amount independent of the assumption used. </run>
                </formatted-text>
                <zone-style>
                  <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                  <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                </zone-style>
              </zone>
            </zone>
          </zone>
