          </zone>
          <zone h='98222' id='6' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='49501' x='49999' y='889'>
            <zone h='23222' id='8' name=' Estimated Profit Margin by Category' pane-specification-id='2' param='[federated.042lfkd0rqc4py103ezla0qwvlf5].[none:Category:nk]' type-v2='color' w='49501' x='49999' y='889'>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='4' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
            <zone fixed-size='635' forceUpdate='true' h='71445' id='9' is-fixed='true' type-v2='text' w='49501' x='49999' y='24111'>
              <formatted-text>
                <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#d3b348' fontname='Algerian' fontsize='14' underline='true'>KEY INSIGHTS:</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='14'>Electronics is the only category with a negative estimated profit margin, around minus 0.10, while every other category is comfortably positive. Beauty leads at roughly 0.42, followed by Fashion at 0.40 and Sports at 0.35.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='14'>Why this matters: revenue and profitability tell opposite stories here. A revenue only view would recommend growing Electronics further. This chart shows the opposite conclusion — Electronics is the weakest performer in the portfolio on a per rupee basis.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='14'>In this the heavier average discounting seen on Electronics is large enough to erase margin entirely and push it negative.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='14'>Note: margin relies on an assumed cost ratio, but Electronics ranking lowest is a robust finding, since it lines up with its discount amount independent of the assumption.</run>
              </formatted-text>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='4' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
