                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#d3b348' fontname='Algerian' fontsize='14' underline='true'>KEY INSIGHTS:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='14'>Electronics is the only category with a negative estimated profit margin, around minus 0.10, while every other category is comfortably positive. Beauty leads at roughly 0.42, followed by Fashion at 0.40 and Sports at 0.35.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='14'>Why this matters: revenue and profitability tell opposite stories here. A revenue only view would recommend growing Electronics further. This chart shows the opposite conclusion — Electronics is the weakest performer in the portfolio on a per rupee basis.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
