        </style-rule>
      </style>
      <size maxheight='1064' maxwidth='1416' minheight='1064' minwidth='1416' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='2' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98496' id='1' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98870' x='565' y='752'>
            <zone h='4229' id='3' type-v2='title' w='98870' x='565' y='752' />
            <zone h='9492' id='4' is-fixed='true' paired-zone-id='5' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard-nav' w='98870' x='565' y='4981' />
            <zone h='84775' id='5' paired-zone-id='4' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard' w='98870' x='565' y='14473'>
              <flipboard active-id='1' nav-type='caption' show-nav-arrows='true'>
                <story-points>
                  <story-point caption='The beggining:Understanding the Dataset' captured-sheet='' id='1' />
                  <story-point caption='Identifying the Research question?' captured-sheet='' id='2' />
                  <story-point caption='The Business, By the Numbers' captured-sheet='Dashboard 1' id='3' />
                  <story-point caption='Which category actually drives the business?' captured-sheet='Dashboard 2' id='4' />
                  <story-point caption='Where is demand concentrated geographically?' captured-sheet='Dashboard 3' id='5'>
                    <capturedDeltas>
                      <worksheet name='Revenue  By State'>
                        <style delta-type='added'>
                          <style-rule element='axis'>
                            <encoding attr='space' class='0' field='[federated.042lfkd0rqc4py103ezla0qwvlf5].[Latitude (generated)]' field-type='quantitative' max='5144350.5392434569' min='-607045.76092527574' projection='EPSG:3857' range-type='fixed' scope='rows' type='space' />
                            <encoding attr='space' class='0' field='[federated.042lfkd0rqc4py103ezla0qwvlf5].[Longitude (generated)]' field-type='quantitative' max='11459493.204835353' min='6703798.4891510671' projection='EPSG:3857' range-type='fixed' scope='cols' type='space' />
                          </style-rule>
                        </style>
                      </worksheet>
                    </capturedDeltas>
                  </story-point>
                  <story-point caption='Isthe revenue  discount revenue gains?' captured-sheet='Dashboard 4' id='6' />
                  <story-point caption='Which categories are actually profitable?' captured-sheet='Dashboard 5' id='7' />
                  <story-point caption='What&apos;s really behind Electronics&apos; dominance?' captured-sheet='Dashboard 6' id='8' />
                  <story-point caption='Is inventory following profit, or just demand?' captured-sheet='Dashboard 7' id='9' />
                  <story-point caption='Where Stock and Profit Disagree' captured-sheet='Dashboard 8' id='10' />
                  <story-point caption='Is performance stable over time?' captured-sheet='Dashboard 9' id='11' />
                  <story-point caption='Do our best customers actually generate better margin?' captured-sheet='Dashboard 10' id='12' />
                </story-points>
              </flipboard>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='87137' id='6' story-point-id='1' type-v2='text' w='155906' x='787' y='16390'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#c290b4' fontname='Algerian' fontsize='16' underline='true'>Introduction: Understanding the Indian E-Commerce Sales Landscape</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>In the world of online retail, revenue growth and profitability don&apos;t always move together, a category can dominate sales and still quietly lose money. For this project, I sought to analyze and visualize e-commerce performance in India using a dataset I sourced from Kaggle, the Indian E-Commerce Sales Analytics Dataset. The dataset contains over 10,000 sales transactions, detailing order value, quantity, discount, shipping duration, and payment mode, alongside 2,000 products across 7 categories with original price, selling price, stock levels, and ratings, and 40,000 customers with demographic and spend history, all reflecting activity across Indian states and cities.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>Each row in the sales data represents a single transaction, offering both micro-level (individual order value, product, discount) and macro-level (category, state, monthly trend) insights. The data was originally compiled to reflect realistic Indian e-commerce activity, and was further structured for analysis and visualization in this report.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>Why This Dataset?</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>In this allows us to intersect revenue performance with profitability and operational efficiency, specifically within the Indian retail context. It opens up rich avenues for analysis:</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>&gt;Which categories actually drive the business, and which ones only look like they do</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>&gt;How discounting behavior affects real profitability, not just top-line sales</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>&gt;Where demand is concentrated across Indian states</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>&gt;Whether inventory decisions are aligned with what&apos;s actually profitable</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>Important note on the data</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>This dataset does not include actual product cost data. Wherever profit margin is shown in this report, it is an estimated figure, calculated using an assumed cost ratio per category. This is clearly labeled throughout as &apos;Estimated Profit Margin.&apos;</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='86618' hidden='true' id='7' story-point-id='2' type-v2='text' w='149409' x='-98' y='14627'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#e799b3' fontname='Algerian' fontsize='15' underline='true'>THE PROBLEM STATEMENT</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>Despite Electronics generating the majority of revenue, there is limited visibility into whether that revenue is actually translating into profit. Categorylevel performance is typically judged by revenue alone, which can hide a very different reality underneath.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>This project seeks to bridge that gap by systematically analyzing sales, discounting, profitability, and inventory behavior across categories, states, and time. By examining revenue concentration, discount patterns, estimated profit margin, and stock allocation, we aim to answer a central problem:</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>Is the business&apos;s revenue growth actually healthy, or is it masking a profitability problem underneath?</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>From this, the following research questions guided the analysis:</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>Key Research Questions:</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>Which category actually drives the business, and is that dominance sustainable?</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>&gt;Why it matters: Reveals whether the business is overly dependent on a single category, and what risk that creates.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>How does discounting behavior affect real profitability, not just revenue?</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>&gt;Why it matters: Distinguishes genuine demand from discount-driven sales volume.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>Which categories are actually profitable once estimated cost is factored in?</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>&gt; Why it matters: Separates categories that look successful from categories that actually are.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>Is inventory allocation aligned with what&apos;s actually profitable?</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>&gt; Why it matters: Identifies whether operational decisions are reinforcing or working against the profitability findings.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>Where is demand concentrated geographically, and is performance stable over time?</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='16'>&gt; Why it matters: Adds operational and regional context to the profitability story. </run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{7F3326A8-FA2D-49F7-AD4C-EAFA178426F9}' />
    </dashboard>
  </dashboards>
